  "instructions": [
    "Combine the rice, water, and 1/2 tsp of the salt in a medium saucepan. Bring to a boil, then cover and cook on low for 15 minutes until the water is absorbed.",
    "While the rice cooks, heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and cook 4 minutes until soft.",
    "Add the turkey to the skillet and break it up with a spoon. Cook 6 to 7 minutes until no pink remains.",
    "Stir in the cumin, paprika, garlic powder, pepper, and the remaining 1/2 tsp salt. Cook 1 minute.",
    "Add the black beans, corn, and salsa. Simmer 5 minutes until the corn is hot and the turkey reads 165 F on a thermometer.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork. Divide the rice among four bowls and top with the turkey mixture.",
    "For leftovers, cool the rice and turkey mixture and store them in airtight containers in the fridge for up to 3 days. Reheat until steaming hot."
  ],
